────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
What the tables are

  The Latin-to-rune mappings, digraph rules, rune-name spellings and glosses
  used by FontVibe's rune pages:
    https://fontvibe.ai/tools/rune-generator              (Elder Futhark)
    https://fontvibe.ai/tools/younger-futhark-translator  (Younger Futhark)
    https://fontvibe.ai/tools/anglo-saxon-runes           (Anglo-Saxon futhorc)

  They are a phonetic approximation for writing modern text in runes, not a
  reconstruction of Old Norse or Old English.

  The runes themselves are an alphabet, not anyone's work. The rune names
  and their glosses are the conventional ones found in popular references;
  nothing in them is claimed as original research.

────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Unicode data

  Code points and character names shown in README.md are produced at build
  time by Python's unicodedata module from the Unicode Character Database
  (https://www.unicode.org/ucd/). They are not stored in this repository's
  data files.

